WEBVTT

00:00:30.250 --> 00:00:32.390
Certainly glad you could join me again today.

00:00:32.390 --> 00:00:35.240
Got your palette set up, let's get going here.

00:00:35.240 --> 00:00:36.840
Let's start off and have them graphically run

00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:38.300
all the colors across the screen

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:39.800
that you need to do this painting with me.

00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:41.340
And they'll come across, as usual,

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:43.000
in the same order that I have them on the palette,

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:45.280
starting with the white and working around.

00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:47.330
While they're doing that, let's go on up here.

00:00:47.330 --> 00:00:48.470
I've already covered the canvas

00:00:48.470 --> 00:00:50.520
with a thin, even coat of liquid white.

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:53.380
It's nice and wet and slick and all ready to go.

00:00:53.380 --> 00:00:56.620
I thought maybe today, let's do a little fall scene

00:00:56.620 --> 00:00:58.300
where maybe the weather's not too great.

00:00:58.300 --> 00:01:00.000
You know, in the fall we have a lot of rainy

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:02.400
and you know the snow's gonna come pretty soon.

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:05.000
So let's do something like that and just have some fun.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:08.940
I'm gonna start out using a small, small amount

00:01:08.940 --> 00:01:12.850
of yellow ochre, just the tiniest little bit,

00:01:12.850 --> 00:01:14.490
a very small amount.

00:01:14.490 --> 00:01:17.570
And right here, sort of make a determination

00:01:17.570 --> 00:01:19.270
where the horizon's gonna be.

00:01:19.270 --> 00:01:22.290
And I'm gonna begin swinging this upward,

00:01:22.290 --> 00:01:24.210
just using strokes like so.

00:01:24.210 --> 00:01:27.590
A little bit more color.

00:01:27.590 --> 00:01:29.860
We'll have a little water in this painting.

00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:33.040
As you know, I'm sort of a water fanatic.

00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:36.340
I like that water, a little yellow in here.

00:01:36.340 --> 00:01:41.600
Okay, I'm gonna go right into some Van Dyke Brown.

00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:44.480
In the same way, just tap the brush into it.

00:01:44.480 --> 00:01:47.270
Okay, let's go right up here.

00:01:47.270 --> 00:01:50.810
And I'm gonna put a little brown right in here.

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:54.820
I'm beginning to create these sky angles.

00:01:54.820 --> 00:01:56.780
Don't let 'em get too straight like this,

00:01:56.780 --> 00:01:59.410
it'll disturb you when it's done.

00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:03.590
Now I'm gonna take brown, and a touch of Prussian blue.

00:02:03.590 --> 00:02:05.730
Let me say that again, a touch.

00:02:05.730 --> 00:02:09.530
Prussian blue is so strong, just a little bit.

00:02:09.530 --> 00:02:12.510
It's brown and blue, okay?

00:02:12.510 --> 00:02:19.270
Now then, just begin bringing that all together.

00:02:19.270 --> 00:02:22.950
Add a touch of the midnight black to it.

00:02:22.950 --> 00:02:25.190
So now we have, in the sky,

00:02:25.190 --> 00:02:28.930
we have a little bit of yellow ochre, some brown,

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:34.990
a little Prussian blue, and some midnight black.

00:02:34.990 --> 00:02:36.280
And we're just gonna sort of work

00:02:36.280 --> 00:02:39.160
all these nice little colors together.

00:02:39.160 --> 00:02:40.790
Try to keep the blue off that yellow

00:02:40.790 --> 00:02:46.980
or you'll get a bright green sky.

00:02:46.980 --> 00:02:48.600
And then, before we start blending that,

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:49.840
we still have a dirty old brush,

00:02:49.840 --> 00:02:51.600
and we'll take some more of the Prussian blue,

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:56.560
a little bit of the black, there we go.

00:02:56.560 --> 00:02:58.280
And let's go ahead and lay our water in.

00:02:58.280 --> 00:02:59.600
Pull from the outside in.

00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:04.420
If you start, if you start from here and go across,

00:03:04.420 --> 00:03:05.630
watch what happens.

00:03:05.630 --> 00:03:08.080
You touch here and go across, you get this big line,

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:10.910
that's bad, and then it's hard to blend out.

00:03:10.910 --> 00:03:13.210
So start from the outside and come over,

00:03:13.210 --> 00:03:14.870
and that way you don't have that harsh line

00:03:14.870 --> 00:03:17.250
that you have to blend out.

00:03:17.250 --> 00:03:20.010
There we go, little tricks like that save you,

00:03:20.010 --> 00:03:21.570
save you a lot of agony.

00:03:21.570 --> 00:03:25.300
We want this to be easy and we want it to work for you.

00:03:25.300 --> 00:03:29.190
Okay, a little bit more of the midnight black

00:03:29.190 --> 00:03:30.000
and crushing blue.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:34.700
mixture, don't want to kill all that nice little yellow area

00:03:34.700 --> 00:03:39.240
that you have 'cause that blue and black will eat it up

00:03:39.240 --> 00:03:42.360
in a heartbeat, 'kay?

00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:44.430
Little darker at the bottom than it is at the top,

00:03:44.430 --> 00:03:49.560
that'll help create your illusion of distance.

00:03:49.560 --> 00:03:54.340
Okay, let me wash the old brush, wash the old brush.

00:03:54.340 --> 00:03:59.800
Shake off the excess.

00:04:01.180 --> 00:04:02.690
That is the fun part.

00:04:02.690 --> 00:04:04.140
Okay, let's go right back up here.

00:04:04.140 --> 00:04:07.080
Now I'm gonna begin blending this together.

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:09.520
Follow the angles in the sky.

00:04:09.520 --> 00:04:13.990
I'm gonna use long strokes and start in the light area

00:04:13.990 --> 00:04:15.610
and work up toward the darker area.

00:04:15.610 --> 00:04:18.090
That way your brush is dirty when it gets to the top.

00:04:18.090 --> 00:04:20.160
Use your clean brush in the light area

00:04:20.160 --> 00:04:23.680
and you can just begin bringing all this together.

00:04:23.680 --> 00:04:26.180
Follow those angles though.

00:04:30.700 --> 00:04:33.170
It's nice and soft.

00:04:33.170 --> 00:04:37.760
Okay, and that gives us a quick, happy little sky.

00:04:37.760 --> 00:04:40.280
Down here, we just go all the way across.

00:04:40.280 --> 00:04:45.320
That straightens out the water and brings it all together.

00:04:45.320 --> 00:04:48.490
We're ready.

00:04:48.490 --> 00:04:52.090
Let me get an old fan brush here.

00:04:52.090 --> 00:04:55.740
I'm gonna mix up, let's take a little black,

00:04:55.740 --> 00:05:00.000
a little brown, a tiny bit of the Prussian blue, and a little

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:03.870
a little bit of alizarin crimson into that.

00:05:03.870 --> 00:05:05.490
I'll put some white here and pull a little bit

00:05:05.490 --> 00:05:07.550
of that into it.

00:05:07.550 --> 00:05:12.410
Maybe I'll add a little more blue to that.

00:05:12.410 --> 00:05:14.430
And a touch more crimson, there we go.

00:05:14.430 --> 00:05:16.180
That's sort of what I'm looking for.

00:05:16.180 --> 00:05:22.010
It's a very dark lavender to the blue side.

00:05:22.010 --> 00:05:24.520
Very dark, it's almost a gray color.

00:05:24.520 --> 00:05:27.360
This is gonna be a gray, cloudy day.

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:29.120
Okay, let me wipe off my knife.

00:05:30.410 --> 00:05:32.320
Now let's take the old fan brush

00:05:32.320 --> 00:05:33.840
and go right through a little bit of color.

00:05:33.840 --> 00:05:35.460
Don't need a lot of paint on the brush this time,

00:05:35.460 --> 00:05:36.760
just a little.

00:05:36.760 --> 00:05:38.700
Add a small amount of brown into that,

00:05:38.700 --> 00:05:41.460
a little more into the brownish color.

00:05:41.460 --> 00:05:42.910
There we go, good.

00:05:42.910 --> 00:05:44.480
Let's go right up here.

00:05:44.480 --> 00:05:47.470
Now back in here, you have to make a decision.

00:05:47.470 --> 00:05:51.370
Maybe there lives some happy little evergreens.

00:05:51.370 --> 00:05:53.820
Just take the corner of the brush,

00:05:53.820 --> 00:05:57.610
just back and forth, just sort of pop in,

00:05:57.610 --> 00:06:00.000
just a little evergreen.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:02.860
some indications of some that are even farther away.

00:06:02.860 --> 00:06:06.970
All we see is just the basic shapes.

00:06:06.970 --> 00:06:10.460
I'm just touching and sort of pulling it downward.

00:06:10.460 --> 00:06:15.420
See, you can make all kinds of little basic shapes.

00:06:15.420 --> 00:06:17.350
Touch, use the top part of the brush

00:06:17.350 --> 00:06:20.160
and just give it a little downward snap.

00:06:20.160 --> 00:06:23.860
There, a little more paint on the brush.

00:06:23.860 --> 00:06:26.050
Maybe over here we got some.

00:06:26.050 --> 00:06:29.060
Be careful, these will get looking like fence posts.

00:06:33.520 --> 00:06:36.900
And to about there, that's good enough.

00:06:36.900 --> 00:06:42.120
Now then, I'm gonna put a few more indications

00:06:42.120 --> 00:06:45.040
of some trees that have a little more shape to 'em,

00:06:45.040 --> 00:06:48.390
and we're just using the corner of the brush

00:06:48.390 --> 00:06:51.670
and just work 'em in, back and forth.

00:06:51.670 --> 00:06:55.150
These little trees live right in your fan brush.

00:06:55.150 --> 00:06:57.560
Sometimes you have to sort of scare 'em out.

00:07:01.850 --> 00:07:11.770
And you just put as many or as few as you want in your world.

00:07:11.770 --> 00:07:15.260
He's got a little friend there.

00:07:15.260 --> 00:07:16.540
Just drop him in.

00:07:16.540 --> 00:07:19.690
Now then, I want to create the illusion of mist back here.

00:07:19.690 --> 00:07:21.650
I want this to be very soft and very distant,

00:07:21.650 --> 00:07:25.330
so we'll take the two-inch brush and tap.

00:07:25.330 --> 00:07:26.770
I'm using the top corner.

00:07:26.770 --> 00:07:29.090
See, look how hard it's hitting, it's bending.

00:07:31.080 --> 00:07:39.930
Really get in here and tap it to create the illusion

00:07:39.930 --> 00:07:44.130
of a very, very soft area back here.

00:07:44.130 --> 00:07:48.370
Even let it come up above some of these here

00:07:48.370 --> 00:07:50.870
to really soften it.

00:07:50.870 --> 00:07:53.350
Trees are already, they're already just lost,

00:07:53.350 --> 00:07:54.260
right in the mist.

00:08:01.920 --> 00:08:04.220
Can you believe how that pushes all that back?

00:08:04.220 --> 00:08:08.570
Just that little tapping action, okay?

00:08:08.570 --> 00:08:12.690
Now then, let's have another plane in the painting.

00:08:12.690 --> 00:08:14.530
And a plane, I mean just another area

00:08:14.530 --> 00:08:15.970
that's closer to you.

00:08:15.970 --> 00:08:17.410
So we'll take those same old colors.

00:08:17.410 --> 00:08:18.410
We'll use some brown.

00:08:18.410 --> 00:08:21.760
I'm gonna put some dark sienna in there this time.

00:08:21.760 --> 00:08:23.600
And a little bit of sap green.

00:08:23.600 --> 00:08:26.070
As things get closer, we'll begin to see

00:08:26.070 --> 00:08:27.150
a little more detail.

00:08:27.150 --> 00:08:29.600
Just a little sap green though, okay?

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:31.240
This brush is really full of paint.

00:08:31.240 --> 00:08:34.080
Let's go right up in here, there it is.

00:08:34.080 --> 00:08:37.710
These trees are a little closer, they're a little bit bigger.

00:08:37.710 --> 00:08:39.580
Look at that.

00:08:39.580 --> 00:08:43.420
Turn that old brush over and use both sides of it.

00:08:43.420 --> 00:08:44.440
There we go.

00:08:44.440 --> 00:08:49.930
This tree's stronger, he's got a little more light.

00:08:49.930 --> 00:08:52.310
Okay, we don't want him to get lonely,

00:08:52.310 --> 00:08:56.150
so we'll give him a friend too.

00:08:56.150 --> 00:09:00.000
Friends are so important, not only to trees, but to us.

00:09:01.820 --> 00:09:05.590
and through painting I have made hundreds and hundreds

00:09:05.590 --> 00:09:07.480
of new friends all over the country,

00:09:07.480 --> 00:09:11.540
and that may be the most rewarding part of all this.

00:09:11.540 --> 00:09:16.290
Most rewarding part.

00:09:16.290 --> 00:09:19.210
I tell you what, here's a happy little tree.

00:09:19.210 --> 00:09:20.230
He lives right there.

00:09:20.230 --> 00:09:23.150
Just sort of visualize in your mind

00:09:23.150 --> 00:09:25.090
where you think the tree would be happy,

00:09:25.090 --> 00:09:28.010
and you put him in there.

00:09:28.010 --> 00:09:30.000
Just put him in there.

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:33.580
bit of the dark sienna and just tap it onto this brush

00:09:33.580 --> 00:09:35.280
and then I want to gather up some of this color

00:09:35.280 --> 00:09:39.090
that we had on the tree and begin very softly

00:09:39.090 --> 00:09:41.210
putting in little hills.

00:09:41.210 --> 00:09:45.400
Look at there, pick up some of that tree color

00:09:45.400 --> 00:09:49.880
and just let it just tap, let it go.

00:09:49.880 --> 00:09:52.500
There's a tiny bit of dark sienna on the brush,

00:09:52.500 --> 00:09:55.870
tiny bit, tiniest little bit.

00:09:55.870 --> 00:09:59.350
See how you can set those trees right up on a little hill?

00:10:00.320 --> 00:10:02.720
and then you begin pulling that down.

00:10:02.720 --> 00:10:07.710
But I want this to be very, very soft, very quiet.

00:10:07.710 --> 00:10:10.400
I like very gentle little paintings.

00:10:10.400 --> 00:10:12.190
And when you're doing yours at home,

00:10:12.190 --> 00:10:13.990
if you want it to be brighter and stronger,

00:10:13.990 --> 00:10:17.140
just use a little stronger color,

00:10:17.140 --> 00:10:26.230
'cause painting is a very individual thing, okay?

00:10:26.230 --> 00:10:29.160
Now, let's go right back into here and load up

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:34.290
just load that fan brush full of paint, okay?

00:10:34.290 --> 00:10:35.310
Tell you what let's do.

00:10:35.310 --> 00:10:38.650
Let's have a tree that lives right there.

00:10:38.650 --> 00:10:43.500
And we take just the corner of the brush,

00:10:43.500 --> 00:10:47.420
begin working him down.

00:10:47.420 --> 00:10:49.040
Then you can just push that old tree

00:10:49.040 --> 00:10:50.770
right out of that brush.

00:10:50.770 --> 00:10:53.540
Little more paint.

00:10:53.540 --> 00:10:55.800
Just push it hard when you get down this far.

00:10:55.800 --> 00:10:58.240
When you first start, you're pushing quite easy.

00:10:58.240 --> 00:11:00.000
By the time you get down here,

00:11:01.080 --> 00:11:04.300
I'm tough with it, strong with it.

00:11:04.300 --> 00:11:07.830
More color, okay.

00:11:07.830 --> 00:11:10.110
I'll tell you what, let's do it right here.

00:11:10.110 --> 00:11:13.320
Big son of a gun.

00:11:13.320 --> 00:11:16.180
See, all these different sizes of trees

00:11:16.180 --> 00:11:18.020
help create the illusion of distance,

00:11:18.020 --> 00:11:26.030
depth in the painting.

00:11:26.030 --> 00:11:30.000
It's beginning to look like fall yet.

00:11:30.030 --> 00:11:42.320
sky, okay, now then I'm gonna go back into a little tiny, tiny, little bit of that dark

00:11:42.320 --> 00:11:47.250
sienna, tiny, can't say that enough times, and I'm gonna create another plane here and

00:11:47.250 --> 00:11:53.100
I'm gonna pick up some of the tree color, see how that, and all I'm doing is just tapping

00:11:53.100 --> 00:12:00.000
the canvas, just tap, and we'll bring it right on across and add the least little

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:03.720
a little touch more of the sienna, look at there.

00:12:03.720 --> 00:12:05.760
See, it creates a whole 'nother plane

00:12:05.760 --> 00:12:07.780
and pushes all those trees back here,

00:12:07.780 --> 00:12:09.700
back into the distance.

00:12:09.700 --> 00:12:13.700
Isn't that super?

00:12:13.700 --> 00:12:16.840
I'm gonna have water here,

00:12:16.840 --> 00:12:20.100
so let's take a little bit of that color

00:12:20.100 --> 00:12:23.880
and just pull it down so we have a little reflection.

00:12:23.880 --> 00:12:26.050
I'm using just a little bit of the dark sienna,

00:12:26.050 --> 00:12:27.410
a little van dyke brown on the brush

00:12:27.410 --> 00:12:30.000
to pull down and create a reflection.

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:35.630
here, just a happy little reflection, there.

00:12:35.630 --> 00:12:41.520
And then lightly go across, okay?

00:12:41.520 --> 00:12:43.440
Now then, I'm gonna take the same old brush

00:12:43.440 --> 00:12:45.780
without cleaning it, just the same old dirty brush,

00:12:45.780 --> 00:12:50.270
and tap right into a little bit of the yellow ochre

00:12:50.270 --> 00:12:56.500
and the bright red, just tap it gently, tap, okay?

00:12:56.500 --> 00:13:00.000
Now then, here, this is a little closer so we're beginning to

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:11.180
see an indication of some highlights and same way, just gently, gently tapping this bright

00:13:11.180 --> 00:13:18.060
red and a tiniest little touch of yellow ochre. Now the red is very strong, be careful with

00:13:18.060 --> 00:13:25.140
it, be careful with it, it'll eat up your whole world in just a second. Take a little

00:13:25.140 --> 00:13:30.000
brown, a little dark sienna mixed together, pull it out, cut across, get that small brown

00:13:30.060 --> 00:13:32.110
of paint right on the edge of the knife.

00:13:32.110 --> 00:13:38.840
Now then, just a little land indication right in there.

00:13:38.840 --> 00:13:41.620
Just like so.

00:13:41.620 --> 00:13:46.830
Just sort of scrubbing across the canvas.

00:13:46.830 --> 00:13:49.970
Tiniest little bit, add a little white

00:13:49.970 --> 00:13:54.480
to that same color, like that.

00:13:54.480 --> 00:13:59.110
And then just an indication of a touch of highlight here.

00:13:59.110 --> 00:14:00.000
I don't want much

00:14:00.540 --> 00:14:03.330
Yes, just a touch here and there.

00:14:03.330 --> 00:14:08.320
Okay, a little bit of the liquid white, cut across it,

00:14:08.320 --> 00:14:13.350
and we'll put just an indication of a little water life.

00:14:13.350 --> 00:14:16.590
Not too much, not too bright.

00:14:16.590 --> 00:14:21.150
Okay, now then go back into my browns.

00:14:21.150 --> 00:14:23.510
Ciena and the Van Dyke.

00:14:23.510 --> 00:14:25.740
And I'm gonna grab some more of this tree color.

00:14:25.740 --> 00:14:28.270
I'm gonna put a little peninsula.

00:14:28.270 --> 00:14:29.890
I think it comes right out here.

00:14:31.790 --> 00:14:33.790
And when you're doing this, just step back,

00:14:33.790 --> 00:14:37.140
look at your painting, and make decisions.

00:14:37.140 --> 00:14:39.820
Just make decisions.

00:14:39.820 --> 00:14:42.260
Pull a little bit of this color down,

00:14:42.260 --> 00:14:48.480
just a little, gently, gently across.

00:14:48.480 --> 00:14:51.470
Now, same old dirty brush,

00:14:51.470 --> 00:14:54.790
back into my yellow ochre and bright red mixture.

00:14:54.790 --> 00:14:58.360
Just a little, same old dirty brush.

00:14:58.360 --> 00:15:00.000
You can get over here and let me

00:15:00.030 --> 00:15:02.750
a little bit of this cad yellow to it, it's alright.

00:15:02.750 --> 00:15:07.450
Now then, follow the angles of the land,

00:15:07.450 --> 00:15:10.810
the lay of the land.

00:15:10.810 --> 00:15:13.810
Just follow it right on down, brighter on top,

00:15:13.810 --> 00:15:16.910
and then darker, darker, darker as it works down.

00:15:16.910 --> 00:15:19.970
If you want to show a little protrusion here.

00:15:19.970 --> 00:15:24.080
See, see, easy that is.

00:15:24.080 --> 00:15:26.060
Creates the illusion of another little hill

00:15:26.060 --> 00:15:29.410
just by changing the value of the color or the intensity.

00:15:30.440 --> 00:15:32.040
A little bit of that right down to the water,

00:15:32.040 --> 00:15:36.300
go across, and you have instant reflections.

00:15:36.300 --> 00:15:37.640
Let's play a little bit over here.

00:15:37.640 --> 00:15:39.160
Tell you what let's do.

00:15:39.160 --> 00:15:41.120
I'm gonna use a round brush and go right into my browns.

00:15:41.120 --> 00:15:44.070
That's the Sienna and the Van Dyke.

00:15:44.070 --> 00:15:46.710
Tap out the excess.

00:15:46.710 --> 00:15:48.660
Okay, let's go up here.

00:15:48.660 --> 00:15:54.320
Maybe back in here there's some happy little trees.

00:15:54.320 --> 00:15:55.980
